This is an independent Rust reimplementation of a subset of Cordis semantics.
It is not an official Cordis, DeepSeek, or Verus distribution.

Design and behavior references:
- Cordis, https://github.com/cordiverse/cordis (MIT)
- DeepSeek Harness, https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness (MIT)
- A Programming Paradigm for Spatiotemporal Composability,
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25512v1 (https://github.com/validation-engineering/cordis-verus/blob/main/reference/README.md)

The ignored upstream checkouts retain their own license and copyright files.
The reference paper is not covered by this project's MIT license.
Verus binaries and vstd retain their upstream licenses. Binary archives are
downloaded into the ignored .tools directory. Project-managed toolchain archives
preserve original upstream bytes with a source/notices companion; see
https://github.com/validation-engineering/cordis-verus/blob/main/docs/toolchains/README.md.
They are separate from Cordis runtime releases.

The experimental JavaScript compatibility package adapts language-layer code
from Cordis (Copyright (c) 2021-present Shigma, MIT). The original MIT notice
is preserved in packages/compat-cordis/LICENSE.upstream. It does not embed the
upstream Fiber lifecycle scheduler. Node-API dependencies retain their own licenses.

The compatibility logger in packages/compat-cordis/logger.js is adapted from
Cordis packages/core/src/logger.ts at the locked Cordis revision. Its formatting,
exporter and traceable-caller behavior are ordinary JavaScript, outside the
Verus proof boundary, and retain the same MIT attribution above.

Windows configuration persistence uses atomicwrites 0.4.4
(https://github.com/untitaker/rust-atomicwrites), under the MIT license:

